---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import Crumbs from '../components/Crumbs.astro';import {siteConfig} from '../site-config.mjs';
---
<Base title={`About ${siteConfig.name}`} description="A free independent educational companion to practitioner material on buying, financing and building businesses." type="About"><Crumbs items={[{title:'About'}]}/><article class="narrow"><header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">Free education. Clear provenance.</p><h1>About {siteConfig.name}</h1><p>{siteConfig.subtitle}</p></header><div class="prose"><h2>Why this site exists</h2><p>Acquisition education is often spread across long conversations, examples and updates. A useful idea about valuation may appear far from a discussion of repayment or operating risk. This site brings related ideas together and makes their source evidence easier to follow.</p><p>The course provides a learning sequence. The reference library supports specific questions. Examples and numbers show the context behind a claim. Original videos are linked prominently so readers can return to the speaker’s full explanation.</p><h2>Free access is part of the design</h2><p>There are no payments, subscriptions, memberships, advertisements, affiliate links or paywalls. No login is required. Optional lesson progress stays in your browser. Static search runs in your browser; search terms are not sent to a site-operated search service.</p><p>Analytics are disabled in this release. The site requests no embedded videos or third-party fonts. Following an external source link takes you to that source’s website and its own privacy practices.</p><h2 id="disclaimer">Independent educational resource</h2><p>{siteConfig.name} is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by {siteConfig.collections['yusufa-sey'].name} or any other referenced creator. It provides original organization, explanation, analysis and commentary based on publicly available educational material. Original videos remain available from their respective creators.</p><p>Source creators retain their original works. The site does not publish the transcript corpus, offer access to recovered audio, or reproduce videos as full written accounts.</p><p>Material is for education. It is not a recommendation to buy a business, approach a particular lender, use a stated valuation, or rely on a legal or tax interpretation. Examples can be simplified, accounts can be anecdotal, and machine-derived evidence can be uncertain.</p><h2>Start with the evidence</h2><p><a href="/methodology/">Read the methodology</a> for the source counts, classifications, transcription limits and editorial boundaries. <a href="/sources/">Explore the original source collection</a> to continue watching.</p></div></article></Base>
